  {
    "sha": "84b70d6bf034fedbc9729d65b759553e2df544a0",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOV1WsOtoAKDg0YjcwZDZiZjAzNGZlZGJjOTcyOWQ2NWI3NTk1NTNlMmRmNTQ0YTA",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-26T18:59:15Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-26T18:59:15Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(tools)!: component library store and project persistence\n\nThe .camproj file now saves the document tool component table\n(components) and each tool's component stack (assembly). The loader\nreads the table and every stack before any world write, checks that each\nlink names a row and that each stack resolves, and lands them through\ntable_set and set_assembly in place of the clear-on-open. The derived\ntool record and body stay as the file states them, so an open never\nshifts a posted program.\n\nA document component can link to a user library copy (library_ref: the\nlibrary id and an FNV-1a content hash). The user component library is\ncamcraft-components/1 in CAMCRAFT_COMPONENTS, else\n<data dir>/camcraft/components/components.camcomponents, read all or\nnothing and saved through a temp file and a rename. The holder library\nand the starter catalog are read-only built-in components. sync_status\ncompares a row with its library copy and never applies it;\nSyncDocumentComponent pulls the copy in and derives every user tool\nagain in one undo step.\n\nThe .camtools export of components is left on #3645.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: the project file steps to v84. A v83 build refuses the\nfiles that this build writes; v83 and older files open unchanged.\n\nRefs #3645\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
