      "message": "feat(ui): tool library window edits user holders and component stacks\n\n#3898 (U7 of #3663), the UI scope of #3648, on the component table of\n#4201 and the user library of #4233:\n\n- \"My library\" is a third source of the tools list: the built-in and\n  user library components by group, a name filter, \"Show compatible\n  parts\" (compatible_parents / compatible_children), and the document's\n  component table with each row's library status and users.\n- A component editor (name, insert code, a holder's gauge length) lands\n  one undoable EditDocumentComponent; every tool built from the\n  component follows in the same undo step. Sync from library, Save to\n  My library and Delete from document stand beside it.\n- A built-in holder copies as a user holder; the Holders page lists the\n  document's user holders.\n- The Tool tab's assembly group shows the tool's component stack:\n  \"Add component\" offers only the parts that fit, Apply stack is one\n  SetToolAssembly, \"Detach to standalone tool\" clears the stack.\n- app re-exports component_fit, frame, insert_iso1832, insert_seat and\n  tool_assembly::Mount for the UI.\n\nA lathe tool's stack waits for #3643. Decisions:\ndocs/decisions/3898-tool-library-components.md.\n\nRefs #3898\nRefs #3648\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
